    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "(front matter / intro)",
      "prov:value": "---\nname: task-authorization\ndescription: >\n  The check every BPMN task execution runs before anything is recorded:\n  is the actor authenticated, assigned to the role the lane binds, authorized\n  by an ODRL policy to perform the task, and allowed access to the content it\n  acts on? One generic check in the engine rather than a step drawn in some\n  diagrams; strict since 2026-09-24, with GitHub as the authenticator. Also how the HTTP\n  routes ask the same policies. Triggers on: may this actor, who may perform,\n  authorization, authentication, access rights, permission check, RBAC,\n  rbac.ts, workflow_complete refused, not eligible for role.\nallowed-tools: Read Grep Glob Bash\n---",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Task authorization — four questions before every task",
      "prov:value": "Issue [#1207](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/1207), a\nchild of #1180. Owner decisions, 2026-09-23, are quoted where they apply.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1207",
        "#1180",
        "issues/1207",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The four checks, in order",
      "prov:value": "It is **one function**, `authorizeTask` in `src/workflow/authorize.ts`, run by\nthe interpreter's `complete()` and by `workflow_gate`. **It is not drawn as a\ntask in any diagram.** A check drawn into some processes is a check missing\nfrom the others, and the owner asked for *\"generic check on each task\nexecution as part of any bpmn engine\"*."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "One action for every task",
      "prov:value": "Owner: *\"Always perform-task.\"* A task asks for `perform-task`, scoped by\n`cat-harness:process`, `cat-harness:task` and `cat-harness:role` constraints\nand by `target`. A step needing a narrower right gets it as a **constrained\nrule in a policy**, never as a new attribute on the diagram:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Authentication is the executor's job, and GitHub is today's authenticator",
      "prov:value": "Owner: *\"process bpmn executor responsibility. its skill, tools may be http but\nwe dont have this setup yet. we do have agentic discussion + git(hub) KG-DS and\nwith github we use it as auth / auth control.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Asking who you are: the `auth_whoami` Tool",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-24: *\"need Tool fo user auth/auth\"*, then *\"do github\"*. The\n`user-auth` Tool node (MCP `auth_whoami`, `src/tools/auth.ts`) answers three\nquestions in one call:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Asking who you are: the `auth_whoami` Tool",
      "prov:value": "**One resolver for preferences and permissions, two thresholds.** The same\nidentities feed both, through `resolveIdentities`\n(`cat-harness-tools/src/core/identity.ts`, bean `f1e1`): GitHub's answer is\nthe one `auth_whoami` gives, and the other providers — GitLab CI, the agent\nhost's account, the user-level store, the git author — are listed beside it,\neach marked vouched or self-asserted. A preference may follow a self-asserted\nidentity\n([`interaction-modality`](../../conduct/conduct-core/interaction-modality.md)\n§3.1). **A permission never does**: only an identity GitHub vouched for maps\nto an actor, and a self-asserted one maps to nobody.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean f1e1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Asking who you are: the `auth_whoami` Tool",
      "prov:value": "**There is no login-to-actor table, and there will not be one.** Owner,\n2026-09-24: *\"just use github accounts and standard personal account\npermission levels\"*. This repository is owned by a personal account, and\nGitHub gives such a repository exactly three levels. They are the whole\nmapping (`PERSONAL_ACCOUNT_LEVELS` in `src/core/github-auth.ts`):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Asking who you are: the `auth_whoami` Tool",
      "prov:value": "**Owner rulings on the analysis, 2026-09-24:**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "GitHub as the auth layer: what it is good at, and where it stops",
      "prov:value": "1. **Where a boundary must hold against a reader, it is a repository\n   boundary.** Sub-graphs with different read audiences belong in different\n   repositories. That is one more reason for the repo split already under way\n   (bean `vuip`).\n2. **Everything finer is ODRL, enforced in process.** The engine's\n   four-check verdict and the HTTP routes govern callers that go through\n   them. **They are not a security boundary against someone who can clone the\n   repository.** Do not describe a scoped ODRL rule as protecting data from a\n   GitHub reader.\n3. **Real per-node or per-query enforcement needs a data store in front of\n   the graph** (the auth-gateway, and later a relationship engine; the owner\n   ruled OpenFGA *later*). The policies do not change when it arrives. Only\n   the place that evaluates them does.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean vuip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "GitHub as the auth layer: what it is good at, and where it stops",
      "prov:value": "## Strict since 2026-09-24, and how it got there",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Strict since 2026-09-24, and how it got there",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-09-24**, across all 628 tasks and gateways in `processes/`,\nwith a GitHub-authenticated principal: `owner` 628 allowed, `collaborator`\n628 allowed, `viewer` 628 refused (`unknown`), nobody 628 refused.\n`scripts/tests/task-authorization-strict.test.ts` pins this, so re-run it\nrather than quoting this paragraph.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The HTTP routes ask the same policies",
      "prov:value": "`src/core/rbac.ts` was a viewer < collaborator < owner ladder, with every route\nhard-coding its minimum rung. Owner: *\"Replace with ODRL now.\"* Now:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The HTTP routes ask the same policies",
      "prov:value": "The gateway policy reproduces exactly what the ladder allowed (every gated\nroute asked for \"collaborator or higher\"), and `task-authorization.test.ts`\npins that."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The engine writes its own PROV-O record",
      "prov:value": "Since 2026-09-24 (bean `n2l9`), `complete()` attaches a `prov:Activity` to\neach history entry it records under an authorization context\n(`src/workflow/prov-record.ts`, `HistoryEntry.prov`):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean n2l9",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "The after-check: the PROV-O QA/QC report",
      "prov:value": "The engine checks **before** a step. An agent swarm acts first, so the same\npolicy is checked **after**, from the record (issue #1180, step 5;\n`docs/source/concepts-agentic-harness/bpmn-execution.md`).\n`scripts/prov-qaqc.ts` reads every instance in `beans/workflows/`, including\nits subprocesses, and for each history entry on an activity or decision:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1180"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The after-check: the PROV-O QA/QC report",
      "prov:value": "- writes one `prov:Activity` (`schemas/content/prov.ts`): `prov:agent` is the entry's\n  actor, `prov:hadRole` is the role the lane binds (`laneBinding`),\n  `prov:hadPlan` is `<process file stem>#<node id>`, and\n  `cat-harness:underPolicy` is every policy evaluated. One log per instance\n  goes to `docs/assets/prov/<instance>.prov.jsonld`;\n- re-runs `authorizeTask` itself. For an entry recorded under a verdict it\n  re-checks **the principal that verdict recorded** (the actor GitHub vouched\n  for); only for an older entry, which records just a name, does it use that\n  name, `asserted`;\n- emits the engine's own `prov:Activity` when the entry carries one, and\n  derives one only for entries that predate it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/task-authorization.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The after-check: the PROV-O QA/QC report",
      "prov:value": "It is **advisory**, unlike the engine, which has been strict since 2026-09-24: findings are listed on the\n`/prov-qaqc/` page and never fail the build. `check:prov-qaqc` fails only on\nstale outputs, a `prov:Activity` that does not validate, or an internal\nerror. Quote the counts from a run, not from the page you remember.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
